MBA Polymers leads plastic recycling from end-of-life durable goods (e-waste, auto shredder residue) through highly automated 20+ step polymer separation technology. Production units across Germany, Austria, China, India, UK process 150,000+ tonnes annually, recovering ABS, PP, PS, HDPE grades as engineered alternatives to virgin plastics. The company monetizes waste-to-feedstock transitions, creating commercial economics for secondary material recovery. Recycled plastics market projected to grow 8.2% CAGR through 2032 (USD 85.9B to USD 149.3B).